MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: ea345e84f819d234cb259efd2a0ed4e8, type: 3}
  m_Name: Husky_InnateSkill
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::Skill
  name: "B\u014Dgyu H\xE9 Assault"
  effect: "Automatically switches between Attack (Assault) and Defense (B\u014Dgyu)
    stances through a player's damage dealing and defend actions."
  triggerCondition: A player using basic attack/damage dealing abilities or defend
    as actions.
  explanation: 'Attack Stance: In the attack stance, basic attacks and damage dealing
    abilities apply a debuff named Hunt (Max of 2 stacks, stacks remain until consumed).

    

    Defense
    Stance: In the defense stance, after receiving a direct attack from an enemy
    within melee range, automatically counterattack that tile.


    The character
    starts combat in the attack stance.

    

    Choosing defend immediately
    enters the defense stance, granting defense effects (refer to Basic Actions)
    and counterattacking the tile the attacking enemy is on.

    

    Only one
    counter between each duelist turn. Counters cannot trigger other counters, switch
    stances, generate energy, count as a turn, or apply Hunt.

    

    The defense
    stance remains until using a basic attack or damage dealing ability, returning
    to the attack stance and applying Hunt while doing so.

    

    In attack
    stance, basic attacks and damage dealing abilities apply Hunt to all enemies
    on the targeted tile, max of one per duelist turn.

    

    Enemies with
    Hunt stacks receive 5% more damage per stack, max of 10%.

    

    Attacking
    a tile where at least one enemy already has 2 Hunt stacks using a basic attack,
    ability, or counter re-uses that move against the whole tile once and removes
    all Hunt stacks from enemies who had 2. Enemies below 2 however gain a stack
    from the original attack, potentially setting up another re-use next turn, unless
    it was a counter. The repeated move does not apply or trigger Hunt and only one
    repeated move can happen per original attack, regardless of how many enemies
    on the tile had 2 Hunt stacks.

    

    Non-damaging abilities, items, and
    movement do not switch stances. Both stances have access to all equipped abilities.'
